&lt;p&gt;
	Since the inspection, the owners have taken direct oversight of the operation and have carried out a comprehensive review of the food safety management systems, staff responsibilities, training, documentation and management controls. The issues identified by the Environmental Health Officers have been treated as a priority and corrective action was taken immediately.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
	The conditions found at the time of the inspection were not typical of the normal conditions maintained at the establishment and arose because:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
	At the time of the inspection, the business was experiencing an unexpected and significant disruption to its management structure. Our General Manager, who had responsibility for overseeing a number of the site&amp;rsquo;s day-to-day operational and compliance procedures, left the business without notice shortly before the inspection. This resulted in an immediate gap in management oversight and, regrettably, a number of food safety management and record-keeping procedures were not being maintained to the standard we expect. Within 48 hours of the inspection, we submitted a formal application for a re-rating inspection, reflecting both the speed with which corrective action was taken and our confidence that the required standards are now being met.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		&lt;em&gt;A new management system has been implemented. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		&lt;em&gt;There is now a new manager and/or new staff. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		&lt;em&gt;The staff have been trained/re-trained/given instruction/are under revised supervisory arrangements.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
